meta {
  name: (8-1) Get Person
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{domain}}/tree/persons/{{person1Id}}/matches?collection=https://familysearch.org/platform/collections/records
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  collection: https://familysearch.org/platform/collections/records
}

docs {
  The /tree/persons/{{personId}}/matches endpoint requests a list of match hints for the person specified by personId. The response may contain match hints from the user tree or the main Family Tree. See the documentation at [https://www.familysearch.org/developers/docs/api/tree/Match_by_Tree_Person_Id_resource](https://www.familysearch.org/developers/docs/api/tree/Match_by_Tree_Person_Id_resource).
  
  Please note that there is some acceptable system latency between when a person is created and their match hints are available via the tree/persons/{personId}/matches endpoint.
  
  If the status code from this request is 204 No Content, no results were found. Wait and allow time for a response of 200 OK. See the example request and response documents at [https://www.familysearch.org/developers/docs/api/tree/Read_Matches_by_Tree_Person_Id_usecase](https://www.familysearch.org/developers/docs/api/tree/Read_Matches_by_Tree_Person_Id_usecase).
  
  If the status code from this request is 200 OK, proceed to (9-1) Get Tree Person IDs.
}
